{
  "raw": {
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/16D5A72295BEEA4BBF29A0DA73DAF892/jobs/155338": {
      "title": "Faculty - English",
      "description": "Faculty - English You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Faculty - English Hot Job Lake Wales, FL 33859 Apply Overview Education Level Graduate Degree Apply Description Position Title: Instructor, Assistant Professor, Associate Professor, or Professor of English Department: Academic Affairs > Communication Arts Position Summary: Warner University is seeking qualified candidates for a full-time English faculty position in the Communication Arts Department for the fall 2026 semester. Responsibilities primarily include teaching Composition and developmental writing courses, though general literature courses may be taught as needed and as opportunities arise. Other responsibilities include student advising and serving on department, college, and university-wide committees. We seek candidates committed to teaching, serving, and supporting the university's mission. The candidate chosen for this position will teach primarily in the traditional, in-person classroom setting at Warner University’s campus in Lake Wales, but may also have opportunities to teach online courses. In keeping with Warner University’s accreditation with SACSCOC and the guidelines provided in the Principles of Accreditation , the university will require the following: Faculty teaching baccalaureate courses: doctorate or master’s degree in the teaching discipline or master’s degree with a concentration in the teaching discipline (minimum of 18 graduate semester hours in the teaching discipline). Faculty teaching graduate and post-baccalaureate coursework: earned doctorate/terminal degree in the teaching discipline or a related discipline. Candidates should hold a minimum of a master’s degree (doctorate preferred) in English or a closely related discipline from a regionally accredited institution. Preference will be given to candidates who have experience in teaching at the college level. The individual must have excellent communication, computer, and organizational skills. Familiarity with Moodle or a similar online learning platform is also desirable. Warner University offers students from diverse backgrounds the opportunity to develop in a Christian environment to their highest intellectual, spiritual, and professional potential. The chosen candidate must affirm and support the university’s Statement of Faith. The successful candidate is expected to display a commitment to Christian education, especially as it addresses the relationship between faith and the study and use of the language in writing and other forms of communication. As such, preference will be given to candidates with some degree of theological education or experience in Christian education within an orthodox, evangelical context. Procedure: Candidates must submit all of the following: a letter of interest a curriculum vitae/resume a faith statement that contains both a personal testimony and a thoughtful response to each paragraph of the university’s official statement of faith ( https://warner.edu/the-university/who-we-are/full-statement-of-faith/ ) copies of all transcripts ( these can be unofficial copies of your transcripts at this time ) the names, titles, and contact information for three (3) to five (5) professional references Applications will not be reviewed unless and until all requested materials are submitted. Applications are being accepted and will continue to be accepted until the position is filled. The contract will start on July 1st, 2026, with a report-on-campus date of August 10 th , 2026. Faculty rank will be contingent on qualifications and experience. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/16D5A72295BEEA4BBF29A0DA73DAF892/jobs/160096": {
      "title": "Facilities Services",
      "description": "Facilities Services - Custodial/Housekeeping You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Facilities Services - Custodial/Housekeeping Hot Job Lake Wales, FL 33859 Apply Apply Description Position Summary The Facilities Services Custodial/Housekeeping employee is responsible for maintaining a clean, safe, and welcoming environment throughout Warner University's campus facilities. Depending on qualifications and experience, this position may be filled as an entry-level employee receiving on-the-job training or as an experienced custodial/housekeeping professional. Responsibilities Clean and sanitize residence halls, classrooms, offices, restrooms, common areas, and other University facilities. Sweep, mop, vacuum, dust, wax, and polish floors and other surfaces as appropriate. Clean windows, lighting fixtures, walls, ceilings, furniture, and other building furnishings. Empty trash and recycling receptacles and transport waste to designated disposal areas. Restock restroom supplies and other custodial inventory as needed. Inspect assigned areas for cleanliness, safety concerns, and maintenance needs, reporting issues to the appropriate supervisor. Assist with setup, breakdown, and cleanup for University events and special projects as assigned. Safely operate and maintain custodial equipment and ensure cleaning tools, supplies, and work areas remain clean and organized. Follow all University safety policies and applicable cleaning, sanitation, and workplace safety procedures. Assist with other Facilities Services duties and special projects as assigned. Qualifications Supportive of Warner University's mission, vision, and core values, with a commitment to a Christian lifestyle and demonstration of character consistent with biblical principles. High school diploma or GED preferred. Previous custodial, housekeeping, janitorial, or facilities experience is preferred but not required. Training will be provided for qualified entry-level candidates. Ability to work independently while also functioning effectively as part of a team. Strong attention to detail, dependability, and customer service skills. Ability to safely lift, carry, push, and move equipment and supplies weighing up to 40 pounds. Ability to stand, walk, bend, stoop, kneel, reach, climb stairs, and perform other physical tasks throughout the workday. Must possess a valid U.S. driver's license and be able to meet the University's Motor Vehicle Record (MVR) standards for authorized drivers. Must maintain reliable transportation for travel between campus buildings as needed. Must be able to receive and respond to work-related communications through a personal mobile device with reliable voice and internet service while performing assigned duties. Ability to successfully complete a background check and any other pre-employment requirements established by the University. Working Relationships The Facilities Services Custodial/Housekeeping employee is a member of the Facilities Services team and reports to the Director of Facilities. Work Schedule Work schedule is determined based on departmental needs and may require occasional evenings, weekends, or support for special campus events. Qualifications Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/16D5A72295BEEA4BBF29A0DA73DAF892/jobs/160057": {
      "title": "Facilities Services",
      "description": "Facilities Services - Maintenance You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Facilities Services - Maintenance Hot Job Lake Wales, FL 33859 Apply Apply Description Position Summary: The Facilities Services Maintenance employee performs general maintenance and repair to help keep Warner University's buildings, grounds, systems, and equipment in safe, functional, and attractive condition. Depending on qualifications and experience, this position may be filled as an entry-level employee receiving on-the-job training or as an experienced Maintenance Technician. Responsibilities: Perform routine maintenance and repair of University buildings, equipment, and campus infrastructure. Assist with or independently perform repairs involving HVAC, plumbing, electrical, carpentry, painting, drywall, masonry, locks, vehicles, small engine equipment, and other building systems based on experience and training. Perform preventative maintenance on facilities, equipment, and mechanical systems. Inspect buildings and equipment for safety, maintenance, and operational concerns. Diagnose maintenance issues and determine appropriate repair methods using experience, technical manuals, blueprints, manufacturer instructions, and other resources. Dismantle equipment or machinery to access defective components and repair or replace parts as needed. Maintain tools, equipment, vehicles, and work areas in a clean, organized, and safe condition. Respond to maintenance requests in a timely, professional, and customer-focused manner. Follow all University safety policies and applicable workplace safety procedures. Assist with other Facilities Management duties and special projects as assigned. Qualifications: Supportive of Warner University's mission, vision, and core values, with a commitment to a Christian lifestyle and demonstration of character consistent with biblical principles. High school diploma or GED preferred. Previous maintenance, construction, facilities, or trade experience is preferred but not required. Training will be provided for qualified entry-level candidates. Mechanical aptitude and willingness to learn building maintenance skills. Experience or certification in HVAC, plumbing, electrical, carpentry, locksmithing, or other skilled trades is strongly preferred for experienced candidates. Ability to safely lift, carry, and move equipment and materials as required. Strong attendance, dependability, and customer service skills. Must possess a valid U.S. driver's license and be able to meet the University's Motor Vehicle Record (MVR) standards for authorized drivers. Must maintain reliable telephone and internet service on a personal mobile device to receive work-related communications while performing assigned duties. Ability to successfully complete a background check and any other pre-employment requirements established by the University. Working Relationships: The Facilities Services Maintenance employee is a member of the Facilities Management team and reports to the Director of Facilities. Work Schedule: Work schedule is determined based on departmental needs and may require occasional evenings, weekends, or emergency response to campus maintenance needs. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/16D5A72295BEEA4BBF29A0DA73DAF892/jobs/161591": {
      "title": "Admissions Specialist",
      "description": "Admissions Specialist You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Admissions Specialist Hot Job Lake Wales, FL 33859 Apply Apply Description Position Summary: Warner University, a Christ-centered institution committed to academic excellence and spiritual formation, seeks a passionate and results-driven Admissions Specialist to join our Admissions team. This role is instrumental in identifying, engaging, and enrolling prospective students who are aligned with the university’s mission and values. The ideal candidate will have a heart for ministry, strong interpersonal skills, and a strategic mindset for outreach and enrollment growth. Responsibilities: Develop and execute recruitment strategies to attract prospective students. Represent the university at college fairs, churches, schools, community events, and other venues across designated regions. Build and maintain relationships with high school counselors, pastors, youth leaders, and other influencers within the community. Serve as the primary point of contact for prospective students from inquiry through enrollment. Conduct admissions calls, campus tours, virtual information sessions, and follow-up communications. Maintain accurate records of prospective student interactions in the CRM (Customer Relationship Management) system. Provide guidance to prospective students and families regarding academic programs, financial aid, scholarships, and the admissions process. Assist in the planning and execution of on-campus recruitment events. Contribute to meeting and exceeding enrollment goals as set by the Assistant Vice President of Enrollment. Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution. Demonstrates a mature and active Christian faith, with a deep commitment to living out biblical values and supporting the mission and spiritual ethos of the university. 1-2 years of experience in recruitment, admissions, sales, or related fields. Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Ability to travel and work flexible hours, including evenings and weekends as needed. Strong organizational skills and attention to detail. Procedure: Along with completing an application, candidates must submit: A resume A cover letter A faith statement that contains both a personal testimony and a thoughtful response to the university’s official statement of faith (https://warner.edu/the-university/who-we-are/full-statement-of-faith/) Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/16D5A72295BEEA4BBF29A0DA73DAF892/jobs/151150": {
      "title": "Online Adjunct Instructor",
      "description": "Online Adjunct Instructor - Natural Science (Biology, Chemistry, Math & Physics) You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Online Adjunct Instructor - Natural Science (Biology, Chemistry, Math & Physics) Lake Wales, FL 33859 Apply Overview Education Level Graduate Degree Apply Description Position Summary: Warner University is accepting applications for its adjunct instructor pool. This pool consists of qualified candidates who may be considered for part-time teaching opportunities when a teaching need arises for online courses. Warner University offers students from diverse backgrounds the opportunity to develop spiritually, academically, and professionally in a Christian environment. Teaching experience in the contexts of evangelical and liberal arts traditions is preferred, and candidates who have some degree of theological education or experience in an evangelical context will be given priority. Individuals must have a minimum of a master’s degree in their discipline. Application Procedure: To be considered for the adjunct instructor pool, candidates must submit the following materials: A letter of interest indicating discipline(s) in which they are qualified to teach A curriculum vitae A faith statement that contains both a personal testimony and a thoughtful response to each paragraph of the university’s official statement of faith (https://warner.edu/the-university/who-we-are/full-statement-of-faith/) Copies of all academic transcripts Names, titles, and contact information for three to five professional references Applications will be kept on file and reviewed as instructional needs arise. Submission of an application does not guarantee placement in an adjunct role. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
