    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/16D5A72295BEEA4BBF29A0DA73DAF892/jobs/159753": {
      "title": "Graduate Assistant Coach",
      "description": "Graduate Assistant Coach - Women's Basketball You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Graduate Assistant Coach - Women's Basketball Lake Wales, FL 33859 Apply Overview Education Level 4 Year Degree Apply Description Position Title:  Graduate Assistant Coach - Women's Basketball Department:  Athletics A Graduate Assistant Coach is expected to affirm and model the Christ-centered mission of Warner University and the Athletic Department. The Graduate Assistant coach must be committed to modeling Christ and leading by example in the lives of our students. Application Requirements: Submit:  Resume - Personal Faith Statement - 2 References Responsibilities: The Graduate Assistant Coach reports directly to the Head Coach or Associate Head Coach of the selected sport and is responsible for assisting in all areas of the program. The GA will also have athletic department and student life responsibilities, as described during the interview process. Qualifications: Supportive of Warner’s mission, vision and core values, commitment to a Christian lifestyle, and demonstration of character in keeping with biblical models. Bachelor’s Degree from an accredited institution required. Strong written and verbal communication skills Ability to work independently, be conscientious and reliable, with an aptitude for creative problem solving. Acceptance into a WU full-time graduate program. Ethical Responsibilities: The Graduate Assistant Coach, as a member of the Athletic Department, agrees to represent the University in an honorable and ethical manner to the best of his/her ability. Standards of ethical conduct for athletic department staff are established and enforced by the Athletic Director, Warner University, the SUN Conference and the NAIA. Work Schedule:  Work schedule varies greatly. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/16D5A72295BEEA4BBF29A0DA73DAF892/jobs/164757": {
      "title": "Head Coach",
      "description": "Head Coach - Strength & Conditioning You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Head Coach - Strength & Conditioning Lake Wales, FL 33859 Apply Overview Level Experienced Position Type Full Time Education Level 4 Year Degree Apply Description Position Title: Strength & Conditioning Coach Department: Athletics Position Summary: The Strength & Conditioning coach is responsible for the development and management of individual and group strength training programs for all men and women student-athletes participating in intercollegiate athletic programs. The Strength & Conditioning Coach is expected to affirm, model, and cultivate the Christ-centered mission of Warner University and the Athletic Department. Responsibilities: Experience running or directly involved with Football strength & conditioning. Develop and manage individual and group weight, strength and fitness training programs. Develop programs by evaluating current physical condition, having a knowledge of the various sports and associated exercises, tailoring strength programs for specific needs, demonstrating proper performance of exercises, correcting mistakes. Monitor progress and provide an assessment of development. Knowledgeable of the sports-related injuries and proper prevention methods; collaborate with athletic training personnel to ensure all preventative and rehabilitation concerns are addressed – staying up-to-date on latest research/methods. Organize lifting schedule for individual and group athletic programs. Select, organize and administer testing procedures in a manner that ensures the collection of valid and reliable performance charts. Daily management and maintenance of the weight room and equipment located in the Tye Athletic Performance Center. Routine meetings with sport coaches. Developing and collaborating with interns. Effectively communicate orally, in writing, and interpersonally. Provide a positive atmosphere that promotes a sense of community and fairness, organization, commitment, motivation, and accomplishment. Attend/Assist with other Warner University events as needed. Work extended days and weekends; ability to travel for athletic events by car, bus or plane (when applicable). Refrain from the use of profanity, obscene gestures, and illegal drugs; be a positive role model on issues of language, alcohol, tobacco, and drugs. Attend and participate in regular department staff meetings. Perform additional duties as assigned by the Athletic Director or Head Athletic Trainer. Qualifications: Supportive of Warner’s mission, vision and core values, commitment to a Christian lifestyle, and demonstration of character in keeping with biblical models. The successful candidate is expected to display a commitment to Christian education, especially as it addresses the relationship between faith and individual/group strength training programs. As such, preference will be given to candidates with some degree of theological education or experience in Christian education within a biblically orthodox, evangelical context. Bachelor’s Degree required, Master’s Degree preferred or an equivalent combination of training and experience in responsible position involving the development and management of sport-specific individual and group strength training programs for men and women (1-3 years’ experience). Requires certification from CSCS or CSCCa, and maintain CPR/AED and First Aid certifications. Experience overseeing or being involved with running multiple programs at once. Exceptional teamwork ability as the position necessitates working closely with coaches and students. Strong motivational skills. Working Relationships: The Strength & Conditioning Coach is a member of the Athletics Department and reports to the Athletic Director. Work Schedule: Work schedule varies greatly depending on lifting schedules; frequent early morning and/or evening work; occasional out-of-town, overnight travel. Candidates must submit all of the following: a letter of interest a curriculum vitae/resume a faith statement that contains both a personal testimony and a thoughtful response to each paragraph of the university’s official statement of faith ( https://warner.edu/the-university/who-we-are/full-statement-of-faith/ ) copies of all transcripts ( these can be unofficial copies of your transcripts at this time ) the names, titles, and contact information for three (3) to five (5) professional references Applications will not be reviewed unless and until all requested materials are submitted. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/16D5A72295BEEA4BBF29A0DA73DAF892/jobs/167024": {
      "title": "Grants and Research Coordinator",
      "description": "Grants and Research Coordinator You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Grants and Research Coordinator Lake Wales, FL 33859 Apply Overview Level Experienced Position Type Full Time Education Level 2 Year Degree Apply Description Position Summary: This position supports the Advancement Office by identifying, researching, and cultivating funding opportunities that advance the mission of the institution. This position is responsible for managing the grant lifecycle, conducting donor and prospect research, maintaining accurate constituent records, assisting with stewardship reporting, and supporting strategic fundraising initiatives. The ideal candidate is highly organized, detail-oriented, an excellent writer, and passionate about advancing Christian higher education through philanthropy. Preference will be given to alumni of Warner University and individuals who have an exceptionally close connection to the institution and/or community. The successful candidate will both understand and value the cultural role of evangelical Christian higher education, and he or she will understand the importance of Warner University in central Florida and beyond. The candidate must affirm and support the University’s official Statement of Faith. The selected candidate must be energetic about the University’s goal of distinguishing itself in the higher-education industry through commitment to historic biblical values. Responsibilities: Research and identify foundation, corporate, government, and private grant opportunities aligned with institutional priorities. Develop and maintain an annual grants calendar with application deadlines, reporting requirements, and stewardship activities. Write, edit, and coordinate compelling grant proposals, letters of inquiry, budgets, and supporting documentation. Collaborate with faculty, staff, and administrators to gather program information, budgets, outcomes, and evaluation data. Prepare timely grant reports and stewardship updates demonstrating donor impact and compliance with grant requirements. Monitor grant expenditures and coordinate with the Business Office to ensure compliance with grant restrictions. Conduct prospect research on individuals, foundations, corporations, and organizations to identify new funding opportunities. Prepare donor profiles, briefing materials, and prospect summaries for the President and Vice President for Advancement. Analyze giving history, wealth indicators, philanthropic interests, and engagement opportunities. Assist in identifying prospective major gift, planned giving, and annual fund donors. Support Advancement with regard to scholarship stewardship, endowment acknowledgments letters , Board of Trustee meetings, and engagement with donors and prospects. Support the team by performing tasks related to organization and strong communication. Assist with advancement projects as needed. Qualifications Associate degree in a related field (bachelor’s degree preferred) The ability to locate and utilize relevant data Commitment to and an understanding of utilizing and providing clean and accurate data Minimum 2 years relevant professional experience in a similar position while demonstrating responsibility for data entry, database management, and gift processing Experience using reporting tools to research and produce reports as requested Experience accepting and recording gifts in a similar not-for-profit organization Experience utilizing Blackbaud Raiser’s Edge or Raiser’s Edge NXT or comparable database tool Excellent verbal and written communication skills, including a professional telephone manner Demonstrated experience in professionally handling sensitive and confidential information Procedure: Candidates must submit the following: Letter of Interest Resume Faith Statement that contains both a personal testimony and a thoughtful response to each paragraph of the University’s official Statement of Faith: ( https://warner.edu/the-university/who-we-are/full-statement-of-faith/ ) Name, title, and contact information for 3-5 professional references Applications will not be reviewed unless all requested materials are submitted. Applications are being accepted and will continue to be accepted until the position is filled. Preferably, the chosen candidate would start in September 2026. Salary will be contingent on qualifications and experience. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/16D5A72295BEEA4BBF29A0DA73DAF892/jobs/168086": {
      "title": "Admissions Recruiting Specialist",
      "description": "Admissions Recruiting Specialist You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Admissions Recruiting Specialist Lake Wales, FL 33859 Apply Overview Level Experienced Position Type Full Time Education Level 4 Year Degree Apply Description Position Summary Warner University is seeking a highly organized, personable, and service-oriented Recruiting Specialist to support the University's enrollment goals by building meaningful relationships with prospective students, families, schools, churches, and community organizations. This position will play an important role in recruiting prospective students and guiding them through the admissions process while creating a welcoming and engaging experience for students and families visiting campus. A key responsibility of this position is managing campus visit logistics, ensuring that individual visits, group visits, tours, and special recruitment events are well coordinated and provide prospective students with a positive introduction to the Warner University community. The ideal candidate is an enthusiastic relationship-builder who can effectively balance student recruitment, communication, event coordination, administrative responsibilities, and attention to detail. Essential Responsibilities Student Recruitment ● Recruit prospective students through phone calls, emails, text messages, social media, personal appointments, school visits, college fairs, and other recruitment activities. ● Develop and maintain meaningful relationships with prospective students, parents, school counselors, pastors, youth leaders, and other influencers. ● Communicate Warner University's academic programs, student experience, campus community, financial aid opportunities, and admissions requirements to prospective students and families. ● Fluently articulate Warner University's commitment to biblical orthodoxy ● Conduct presentations and represent Warner University at high schools, college fairs, churches, community events, and other recruitment activities. ● Follow up consistently with prospective students throughout the recruitment and admissions process. ● Maintain accurate and timely records of recruitment activities, communications, and prospective-student interactions in the University's CRM or student information system. ● Assist with recruitment events and other enrollment initiatives. Campus Visit Coordination ● Serve as a primary point of contact for prospective students and families scheduling campus visits. ● Coordinate details pertaining to campus visits with Assistant Director of Traditional Enrollment. ● Coordinate with admissions staff, faculty, coaches, student ambassadors, residence life, financial aid, academic departments, and other campus partners to ensure a seamless visit experience. ● Maintain campus visit calendars and ensure appropriate staffing and resources are available for scheduled visits. ● Welcome prospective students and families and help ensure they feel informed, valued, and connected to the Warner University community. ● Follow up with visitors after their campus experience to encourage continued engagement and answer questions. ● Monitor campus visit activity and provide recommendations for improving the prospective-student experience. Administrative & Team Responsibilities ● Assist with the development and execution of recruitment plans and enrollment initiatives. ● Participate in admissions team meetings, training, professional development, and strategic planning. ● Collaborate with university departments to create a consistent and positive prospective-student experience. ● Assist with recruitment materials, communications, presentations, and special projects. ● Travel as needed for recruitment activities, including occasional evenings and weekends. ● Maintain confidentiality of student information and comply with applicable University policies and regulations. ● Perform other duties as assigned in support of the University's enrollment and student recruitment objectives. Required Qualifications ● Bachelor's degree from an accredited institution. ● Excellent written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. ● Strong organizational and time-management skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines. ● Demonstrated ability to build positive relationships with students, families, and professional colleagues. ● Strong attention to detail, particularly in scheduling and event coordination. ● Ability to work independently while also functioning effectively as part of a collaborative team. ● Willingness and ability to travel and work occasional evenings and weekends as required by recruitment activities and campus events. ● Valid driver's license and ability to travel for recruitment purposes. Procedure: Candidates must submit the following: Letter of Interest Resume Faith Statement that contains both a personal testimony and a thoughtful response to each paragraph of the University’s official Statement of Faith: (https://warner.edu/the-university/who-we-are/full-statement-of-faith/) Name, title, and contact information for 3-5 professional references Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/16D5A72295BEEA4BBF29A0DA73DAF892/jobs/168818": {
      "title": "Director of Facilities Services",
      "description": "Director of Facilities Services You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Director of Facilities Services Lake Wales, FL 33859 Apply Overview Level Management Position Type Full Time Education Level 4 Year Degree Category Facilities Apply Description Position Title: Director of Facilities Services Department: Facilities Services Position Summary: This position oversees the functions of the Facilities Services department including maintenance, housekeeping and grounds. The Director of Facilities Services will supervise all department staff; ensure proper maintenance of all buildings and grounds; and provide an aesthetically pleasing, clean and functional learning environment in support of the strategic mission and goals of the university. Responsibilities: Provide vision and strategic direction for the Facilities Services department. Supervise and direct facilities services staff and work-study students; and mentor, coach and evaluate staff performance. Model and encourage an environment of excellent customer service among all facilities personnel. Develop and implement methods to monitor and track work orders and service requests. Manage and prioritize annual budgets for all functional areas of the department. Work closely with architects, engineers, design professionals and university leadership on any new building construction or renovation. Participate in the development of long-range campus master plans. Other duties as needed. Qualifications: Supportive of Warner’s mission, vision and core values, commitment to a Christian lifestyle, and demonstration of character in keeping with biblical models. A minimum of five years of experience in facilities management. Possess in-depth technical knowledge/expertise of engineering, construction, maintenance, facility and general management. Have knowledge of applicable federal, state, and local legislative and regulatory requirements including building codes, OSHA regulations and safety requirements. High level of interpersonal skills and ability to handle confidential situations and documentation . Bachelor's degree from an accredited institution. Experience working in an education environment (preferably higher education). Procedure: Candidates must submit all of the following: a letter of interest a curriculum vitae/resume a faith statement that contains both a personal testimony and a thoughtful response to each paragraph of the university’s official statement of faith ( https://warner.edu/the-university/who-we-are/full-statement-of-faith/ ) copies of all transcripts (these can be unofficial copies of your transcripts at this time) the names, titles, and contact information for three (3) to five (5) professional references Working Relationships: The Director of Facilities Services is a member of the Facilities Services Department and reports to the Assistant Vice President for Technology and Facilities. Work Schedule: Normal office hours expected Monday through Friday.  Additional hours as needed for significant department or university events. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/16D5A72295BEEA4BBF29A0DA73DAF892/jobs/170769": {
      "title": "Head Coach",
      "description": "Head Coach - Club Sports and Intramurals You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Head Coach - Club Sports and Intramurals Lake Wales, FL 33859 Apply Overview Level Experienced Education Level 4 Year Degree Apply Description Position Title: Head Coach—Club Sports and Intramurals Department: Student Life Position Summary: This position supports Warner University’s recruitment, retention, student development, and educational ministry efforts by providing leadership, instruction, and oversight for the University’s club sports and intramural programs. The Head Coach—Club Sports & Intramurals will serve as the primary coach and instructor for designated club sports, leading practices and teaching sport-specific skills, strategies, rules, sportsmanship, teamwork, and personal development. The position is also responsible for the administration and continued development of the University’s club sports and intramural programs, including establishing program goals and procedures, evaluating student participation and program needs, developing competitive and intramural schedules, managing program resources, and recommending changes or expansion based on student interest and institutional priorities. The primary purpose of these programs is to provide meaningful opportunities for student instruction, discipleship, leadership development, recruitment, retention, and campus engagement. This position serves as the University’s primary resource for club sports and intramural programming and exercises judgment in the day-to-day administration of assigned programs. This is a full-time, 12-month position reporting to the Vice President of Student Life and working closely with Student Life, Admissions, Athletics, Student Financial Services, and other University departments. The ideal candidate will be highly organized, detail-oriented, and passionate about the cause of gospel-centered, biblically orthodox higher education. He or she will both understand and value the cultural role of Christian higher education. Additionally, the selected candidate must be energetic about the University’s goal of distinguishing itself in the higher-education industry through commitment to historic biblical values. Most importantly, the chosen candidate will have a heart for student ministry and the work of discipling others in the Christian faith. The chosen candidate must affirm and support the University’s official Statement of Faith. Responsibilities: Support the mission and core values of Warner University and Student Life through the leadership and administration of club sports and intramural programming. Create, implement, and personally model a spiritual-formation plan focused on Jesus for students participating in club sports and intramural activities. Serve as the primary coach and instructor for assigned club sports, including planning and conducting practices and providing direct instruction in sport-specific skills, techniques, strategies, rules, teamwork, sportsmanship, and personal development. Coordinate practice planning, skill development, and coaching strategies that prepare participants for competition and continued growth. Provide a positive program environment that promotes community, fairness, organization, commitment, motivation, accountability, and accomplishment. Establish and enforce standards of conduct for club sport participants and provide mentoring designed to foster spiritual, athletic, academic, emotional, and social development. Direct the recruitment and retention efforts for club sport participants, including identifying prospective students, communicating program opportunities, and working collaboratively with Admissions and Student Life to support enrollment goals. Develop, administer, and evaluate the University’s club sports and intramural programs in alignment with institutional goals and student needs. Evaluate current and proposed club sports and intramural offerings and make recommendations regarding the creation, modification, continuation, or discontinuation of programs. Establish competitive schedules for club sports and identify appropriate institutions and organizations for competition. Coordinate travel, hosting arrangements, facilities, and other logistical needs for practices, contests, and program activities. Develop and oversee the University’s intramural calendar, including determining appropriate sports, formats, schedules, and participation structures based on student interest and available resources. Manage approved operational, equipment, and scholarship budgets while demonstrating fiscal responsibility and compliance with University guidelines. Oversee the purchase, maintenance, inventory, and collection of equipment and other resources used for club sports, intramurals, and campus game-room activities. Maintain accurate records related to student participation, program activities, disciplinary matters, budget utilization, equipment, and other relevant program information. Assess student participation, retention, and program effectiveness and recommend changes designed to improve student engagement and program outcomes. Collaborate with Student Life, Admissions, Student Financial Services, Marketing, Facilities, and other University departments to support program operations, recruitment, student development, and campus engagement. Work with Marketing to develop promotional strategies and content related to club sports, intramurals, recruitment, and student participation. Prepare program assessments, reports, recommendations, and budget information for the Vice President of Student Life and other institutional leadership. Attend and participate in Student Life staff meetings and other University meetings as requested. Perform additional duties as assigned by the Vice President of Student Life. Qualifications Bachelor’s degree required; degree in recreation, sports management, ministry, education, student affairs, or a related field preferred. Previous experience in coaching, recreation, club sports, intramurals, student activities, athletics, student ministry, or a related student-development environment. Demonstrated ability to coach, instruct, mentor, and develop students in a structured team or recreational setting. General knowledge of a variety of recreational and club sports, including activities such as cornhole, table tennis, kickball, pickleball, archery, billiards, and similar programs The ability to develop meaningful relationships with students while maintaining professional boundaries Ability to work a flexible schedule, including evenings, weekends, practices, competitions, and special events as needed. Must possess a valid U.S. driver's license and be able to meet the University's Motor Vehicle Record (MVR) standards for authorized drivers. Excellent verbal and written communication skills, including a professional telephone manner Demonstrated experience in professionally handling sensitive and confidential information Procedure: Candidates must submit the following: Letter of Interest Resume Faith Statement that contains both a personal testimony and a thoughtful response to each paragraph of the University’s official Statement of Faith: ( https://warner.edu/the-university/who-we-are/full-statement-of-faith/ ) Name, title, and contact information for 3-5 professional references Applications will not be reviewed unless all requested materials are submitted. Applications are being accepted and will continue to be accepted until the position is filled. Preferably, the chosen candidate would start in October or November 2026. Salary will be contingent on qualifications and experience. Share job details to Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    }
  },
